    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok, but you're basically saying the 'pro-privilege' side is more defensible. if i'm arguing the other way—that it's an erosion of checks and balances—what's the actual legal weakness in that argument? does it just rely on being too 'idealistic' compared to the reality of the presidency?",
